<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves rise to $1.626 bln on Sept 20.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves rise to $1.626 bln on Sept 20.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $1.626 billion on September 20, up $39 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In the previous week to September 13, international reserves fell $6 million.</p>
<p>Central Bank did not give an explication for the growth of reserves.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $1.556 billion.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito newsroom, 5932 258-433</p>
